// PENDING: a boundary parameter of BARE `[u8; 7]` omits the machine's unit
// plan at `call operation: boundary arguments`, with no diagnostic — the
// program is refused with the downstream "selected ProgramEntry
// establishment rejoins 0 Terminal attachment identities".
//
// The cause is one token. `byte_sequence_carrier`
// (`04_typed-trees-to-checked-trees/src/execution/terminal_unit/types/mod.rs`)
// recognizes an OWNED `[u8; N]` as a byte-sequence carrier only when it
// carries a DOMAIN; a borrowed `&[u8]` needs none. Without one the formal is
// a closed primitive array, and `trait_boundary_call.rs` returns None
// outright before it plans any argument.
//
// Measured as a pair. This program omits. The same program with
//
//     pub domain [u8; 7]::CName requires self[6] == 0;
//     ... take(name: [u8; 7] in CName) ...
//
// instead reports "cannot prove requires contract for call take from
// Main::main: self.buf in `[u8; N]::CName`" — an honest, actionable
// refusal naming the obligation the caller has not discharged. So the
// domain-carrying spelling is the supported one and the compiler engages
// with it properly.
//
// This is why all three `samples/gui/{image_viewer,window_app,window_demo}`
// omit at the same phase and nothing else in the tree does: each declares
// `Gui::window_create(class_name: [u8; 7], title: [u8; 11], ...)` with bare
// arrays. Their repair is a carrier domain, which is `samples/gui`'s owner
// to spell.
//
// The bare form deserves a diagnostic rather than an omission, but that
// refusal cannot live in the planner: a `return None` there means "this
// machine has no unit plan", and a machine whose plan nobody needs must
// stay silent. It belongs in a validation pass over boundary declarations,
// which is why this is pinned rather than patched.
//
// Promote to `pass/providers/` with an exit when a bare closed primitive
// array is either planned or refused by name.
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

pub boundary trait Sink { machine take(name: [u8; 7]) -> u64; }

pub data SinkProvider { seen: u64; }

pub macos_arm64 machine SinkProvider::provider_defaults(defaults: &mut SinkProvider) {
    defaults.select_provider<Sink, SinkProvider>();
}

pub macos_arm64 machine SinkProvider::take(name: [u8; 7]) -> u64 satisfies Sink::take {
    transition { _ -> ret() }
    state ret() -> u64 { 7 }
}

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    sink: Binding<Sink>;
    buf: [u8; 7];
    out: u64;
}

machine Main::main(&mut self) reaches Console + Sink {
    self.out = self.sink.take(self.buf);
    self.console.exit_process(0);
}
